  "article_opening": "Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe\nJuly 2, 2026 -- Today’s top stories: Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe, Rubio Would Step Aside for Vance in 2028 White House Race, and Google Ordered To Pay Klarna $1.97b in Antitrust Damages.\nBy CommonWealth Magazine\nSingapore seizes $42m home in Nvidia chip smuggling case\nSingapore authorities have seized a multimillion-dollar mansion and charged people with money laundering as part of a case of suspected c",
  "passage": "Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe\nJuly 2, 2026 -- Today’s top stories: Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe, Rubio Would Step Aside for Vance in 2028 White House Race, and Google Ordered To Pay Klarna $1.97b in Antitrust Damages.\nBy CommonWealth Magazine\nSingapore seizes $42m home in Nvidia chip smuggling case\nSingapore authorities have seized a multimillion-dollar mansion and charged people with money laundering as part of a case of suspected cross-border smuggling of hardware containing Nvidia chips.\nA prohibition of disposal order was issued against the luxury home, valued at about SGD 55M ($42M), freezing the asset and preventing its purchase or sale. Funds in bank accounts under investigation, valued at about SGD 1M, were also seized.\nLim Jenny and Woon Guo Jie Aaron, two people suspected of involvement in the alleged smuggling, face money laundering charges. Four firms allegedly linked to the export of computer servers that might contain Nvidia chips to Malaysia are facing charges for false representation.\nThe companies are Aperia International, A-Speed Infotech, and Aperia Cloud Services (II) — collectively known as the Aperia group — and Luxuriate Your Life.\nThis comes after a US investigation into whether Chinese start-up Deepseek had circumvented US restrictions on advanced Nvidia chips by buying them from third parties in other countries, including Singapore.\nLuxuriate Your Life was charged on July 1, while the oth",
  "statement": "A prohibition of disposal order was issued against the luxury home, valued at about SGD 55M ($42M), freezing the asset and preventing its purchase or sale. Funds in bank accounts under investigation, valued at about SGD 1M, were also seized."
